following multiple delays dying light 2  stay human is finally releasing on a  console or pc near you and to prepare  you for all the zombie killing parkour  action that the game has to offer we've  rounded up a bunch of things you need to  know for more dying light videos make  sure you're subscribed to gamespot  dying light 2 stay human is a first  person open world action adventure game  set 20 years after the events of the  first dying light as a brief refresher  for that game there was a deadly virus  that turned those infected into  dangerous zombies it was contained in  the isolated city of haran which  effectively controlled the spread of the  virus for a while until a new strain  escaped the laboratory and eliminated 98  of the world's population modern  civilization as we know it came to an  end pushing humanity into a new dark age  playing as kyle crane an undercover  agent determined to find intel on the  virus you parkour your way around her on  hacking zombies making makeshift weapons  and helping any survivors  in dying light 2 you are no longer kyle  crane instead you play as aidan caldwell  a member of the pilgrims a group of  freelance runners who travel around the  world handling various jobs for people  while risking their lives among the  hordes of infected when we meet aiden he  is headed to the city it does have a  real name it's just more commonly  referred to as the city and he's on a  quest to find his sister mia they were  both a part of mysterious experiments as  children but were tragically separated  during a fire now aiden is haunted by  that past and wants to know exactly what  those scientists were up to as well as  whether or not his sister is still alive  after the global outbreak a few  settlements remained but vilador aka the  city is the largest the city is a  fictional european location based on  turkish and islamic cities that is four  times larger than the world of the  original game within the city you'll be  able to take on side missions explore  abandoned buildings and make essential  choices that will impact the flow of  your story throughout the game aiden  will rub shoulders with various factions  in the city and at critical points in  the plot he'll need to choose whom to  side with those factions include the  survivors who want to establish safe  zones and adapt the renegades  ex-prisoners that want to rule the city  and the peacekeepers loyal soldiers  trying to enforce their version of the  law depending on which factions control  the districts of the city you'll see  changes to the environment that reflect  their ideologies for example choose to  help the survivors and they might build  a school on a rooftop to teach children  however if you choose to help the  peacekeepers instead they'll build an  outpost with a shopkeeper and npcs with  missions for you  similar to the first dying light the  creatures you fight are light sensitive  making it much safer to travel by  daylight than at night however that also  means you're likely to run into nests of  zombies in interior locations making  exploration hazardous stay human also  welcomes multiple new types of special  infected like sleeping beauties  revenants and banshees sleeping beauties  are infected that linger in dark areas  in a drowsy state forcing the player to  sneak around them make too much noise or  shine your flashlight at them for too  long and you risk getting overrun by a  group banshees on the other hand are  quick and often cause me to feel like my  dodging skills need a ton of work but  despite the new monsters to fear and  stay human the volatile is still one  that freaks me out and gets my heart  racing every time it's insanely powerful  and horrifying to look at why couldn't  they have just gone extinct in between  games the dying light series puts a big  emphasis on traversal providing you with  parkour abilities so you can make your  way through its desolate urban landscape  quickly and effectively and stay human  parkour gameplay has been expanded to be  more natural and intuitive to learn some  of these changes include a slow motion  effect and enhanced time in the air  during jumps to compensate for how a  player can't rely on their natural  agility and expanded vision to make  acrobatic decisions on the fly aiden has  athletic conditioning and can maintain a  brisk pace of 14 miles per hour while he  performs various parkour moves  according to the lead game designer  parkour is designed to be both easy to  learn and hard to master and is largely  unaffected by dying light 2's difficulty  modes not including fall damage  modifiers on more challenging settings  there are 24 park horse skills and stay  human for aiden to acquire including  significant jump upgrades wall running  and bashing through enemies without  stopping there are also 24 combat skills  that can be unlocked these include block  charge which as the name suggests  involves you charging at an enemy while  blocking and knocking them to the ground  perfect parry that staggers an enemy  when you block at the last minute and  ground pound a powerful attack while in  midair advanced technology is scarce in  dying light 2 and firearms are hard to  come by requiring you to scavenge parts  and craft makeshift weapons in order to  survive the onslaught of infected along  with enemy factions looking to take what  you have  you'll see some ranged combat as well as  first person melee fighting which will  feel very familiar if you played the  first game in some instances you can  build modded weapons that have multiple  uses along with that modded weapons are  far more effective in the sequel but  your enemies are also far more capable  of taking you down in combat there's  been a lot of hubbub around how long the  game takes to complete according to  teclan a focused playthrough of dying  light 2's main story can be finished in  around 20 hours to complete side quests  learn about the lore and speak with all  the game's characters you'll need about  80 hours and to completely 100 the game  you'll need to devote around 500 hours  of your life adding to this the studio  revealed that the game's script contains  350 000 words amounting to around 40 000  lines of dialogue so essentially if you  stick around for all 500 hours you can  expect to hear all 40 000 lines and if  that isn't enough tecline also said it  is committed to five years of game  support for dying light 2. with this  fans can expect quote more story dlcs  more events more locations and more  in-game items and you don't have to face  the hordes of infected alone dying light  2 will support up to 4 player co-op as  an added twist a party can vote on key  choices that will be made throughout the  campaign although the host of the party  will ultimately have the deciding vote  if you join a friend for a co-op session  all character progress and items earned  will follow you back to your own game  after a co-op session has ended dying  light 2 stay human is set for release on  february 4th 2022 for pc playstation 5  ps4 xbox series xns and xbox one  everyone who buys dying light 2 on ps4  can upgrade to the ps5 edition at no  extra cost additionally dying light 2  supports microsoft's smart delivery  platform which means those who buy the  game on xbox one get it on series x and  s for nothing extra unfortunately  techland announced that cross-platform  and cross-progression co-op play is not  supported at launch on console however  cross play between users on steam and  the epic game store for pc will be  available from day one the game will  also be available on nintendo switch via  cloud streaming however nintendo players  will have to wait a little longer for  that version as it was delayed on  january 19th and is now slated to arrive  sometime within six months of february  4th and there you have it everything you  need to know before becoming aiden and  fighting to stay human dying light 2 has  a ton to do and seems to be a great  world to get lost in if having the  constant threat of being eaten is your  kind of thing so hit the like button if  you've enjoyed this video and then head  over to the comment section and let us  know if you're excited for dying light  2. do you plan on playing it for 500  hours or will another one of february's  big releases pull you away thanks for  watching
 

